      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-15384",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "A thermometer is placed into a water bath and displays a reading of ${50}^{\u2218}C.$ The thermometer is then transferred to a ${10}^{\u2218}C$ water bath, and its reading begins to decrease. After $5$ minutes, the thermometer reading is ${40}^{\u2218}C.$ To the nearest minute, how long does it take for the thermometer to register a reading of ${30}^{\u2218}C?$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that the temperature reading $T(t)$ of the thermometer decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling, where $T$ is measured in degrees Celsius and $t>0$ is the time, in minutes, since the thermometer was transferred into the ${10}^{\u2218}C$ water bath.*",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066127/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "67b4c4d78355bc6c4c4559e1f2703de5e813d430e2fd09822daf409e9474acf3"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2177,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
